WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:00.763
Welcome.

2
00:00:00.763 --> 00:00:03.977
This briefing comes from
DNS, DHCP and IPAM,

3
00:00:03.977 --> 00:00:07.975
one of the books of the
Federal Modernization Workbook.

4
00:00:07.975 --> 00:00:12.411
It's about governing the name and
address layer as one control plane,

5
00:00:12.411 --> 00:00:15.975
across the data center, every
cloud and the branch edge.

6
00:00:15.975 --> 00:00:20.212
That may sound like plumbing, but here's
the idea that drives the whole book.

7
00:00:20.212 --> 00:00:22.350
Every connection starts with a name.

8
00:00:22.350 --> 00:00:25.650
So whoever governs the name
layer governs the enterprise.

9
00:00:25.650 --> 00:00:29.471
We'll go in four steps: why
DNS is now the control plane,

10
00:00:29.471 --> 00:00:33.825
what has to change, who owns it,
and how to migrate it and run it.

11
00:00:33.825 --> 00:00:38.635
Along the way you'll hear about failures
that don't look like DNS failures at all,

12
00:00:38.635 --> 00:00:41.225
which is exactly why
they're so hard to find.

13
00:00:41.225 --> 00:00:42.530
Let's start with why.
